{"event_type":"review","id":"981b16012815928ce4b49755a85c5c2e9f20ce13c78c3f16aa57c6afdf8e3da5","occurred_at":"2026-11-16T04:57:51Z","payload":{"artifacts":[{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/d19b1b9db7509f8583d52bc9211b4d838d3ea7355d6572ec02dfd4212bb07a2c","sha256":"d19b1b9db7509f8583d52bc9211b4d838d3ea7355d6572ec02dfd4212bb07a2c"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/6190b5e425664b62b445dfe12ab1c8716901bbdca1b376398c41d71e2e6a1c45","sha256":"6190b5e425664b62b445dfe12ab1c8716901bbdca1b376398c41d71e2e6a1c45"},{"kind":"git-bundle","location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/141a2d60ab74afbf9a38133e42ec1b776de4942872779c510605d36ea1084f7b","sha256":"141a2d60ab74afbf9a38133e42ec1b776de4942872779c510605d36ea1084f7b"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/d79315833792b90c4ab4ff26ded21d407a26d35c185a4fa1762d93b0454ffc7a","sha256":"d79315833792b90c4ab4ff26ded21d407a26d35c185a4fa1762d93b0454ffc7a"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/d2c9b91c1f2e3c08df0d5123e20fd5d3b049a2886091e264be8e4632e49f2a1e","sha256":"d2c9b91c1f2e3c08df0d5123e20fd5d3b049a2886091e264be8e4632e49f2a1e"}],"attempt_id":"459a3c6e9123e37cf4b3bafa52986ab893229a9a62b3361e08bc14d384fad28d:0:1","base":"fd4ae9a9c7d6444093e49306a06084f28f09ffc8","completion":{"errors":[],"exit_code":0,"scope_verified":true,"skipped":false,"terminal":true},"findings":[{"anchor_status":"verified","blob":"86b91ed487249d9fa6081978ca26655969c7e154","body":"**Do not infer directory durability from file existence.**\n\nIn `src/adapters/store/nonceLedger.ts:122`, a new instance skips directory sync whenever the file exists.\n\nIf an earlier instance creates the file but fails before directory sync, its error path removes the append lock and leaves the file. A new instance then appends another nonce and returns `consumed` without syncing the directory. File synchronization alone does not guarantee that the directory entry survives a system crash. Losing that entry can permit replay. ([man7.org](https://man7.org/linux/man-pages/man2/fsync.2.html))\n\nSync the directory before the first successful consumption in each instance, even when the file already exists.","id":"77f06c7a7f3a7fbbbf441456b824ecdcdb22fc67b94887653d2c40acb2140f46","intervals":[[122,122]],"path":"src/adapters/store/nonceLedger.ts","severity":"major","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Do not infer directory durability from file existence."},{"anchor_status":"verified","blob":"86b91ed487249d9fa6081978ca26655969c7e154","body":"**Persist newly created ledger directories.**\n\nIn `src/adapters/store/nonceLedger.ts:281`, recursive `mkdir` can create the ledger's parent directory. For `/state/new/nonces`, the later sync covers `/state/new`, but no sync covers the new entry in `/state`.\n\nDirectory entries require synchronization of their containing directory. A system crash can therefore lose the new directory and its ledger after `consume` returns `consumed`, which can permit replay. ([man7.org](https://man7.org/linux/man-pages/man2/fsync.2.html))\n\nPersist each newly created directory entry in its parent, or require a pre-created durable ledger directory.","id":"144830cba9a1d28a386410d09cc8463ffb488dde196c0a22d5f6542d1a74553c","intervals":[[281,281]],"path":"src/adapters/store/nonceLedger.ts","severity":"major","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Persist newly created ledger directories."}],"head":"52fdc77131f46d36444efe64056bc592a8a1847b","head_tree":"7e3bc6040d8da1acb2564424b853efe795537180","input_scope":[{"blob":"86b91ed487249d9fa6081978ca26655969c7e154","intervals":[[1,400]],"path":"src/adapters/store/nonceLedger.ts"}],"job_id":"459a3c6e9123e37cf4b3bafa52986ab893229a9a62b3361e08bc14d384fad28d:0","outcome":"completed","paths":[{"baseline":{"method":"projection","reason":"path cluster"},"blob":"86b91ed487249d9fa6081978ca26655969c7e154","disposition":"included","mode":"100644","path":"src/adapters/store/nonceLedger.ts","reason":"bounded verified input"}],"policy_digest":"eacd1bcf42a0e72eca72fcf9c1e9c8f97e7c515cd67a8fa7965c966924647693","repo":"camerontaylor/cq-toolkit","requested_scope":[{"blob":"86b91ed487249d9fa6081978ca26655969c7e154","intervals":[[140,152]],"path":"src/adapters/store/nonceLedger.ts"}],"reviewed_scope":[{"blob":"86b91ed487249d9fa6081978ca26655969c7e154","intervals":[[140,152]],"path":"src/adapters/store/nonceLedger.ts"}],"scope_digest":"1675c601da1c5d2c55f8768bf271784cfaa43cc83f716c5cb49319cda11e5ee6","source":{"authenticated":true,"id":"backfill-459a3c6e9123e37cf4b3bafa52986ab893229a9a62b3361e08bc14d384fad28d-g0-20261116T045216Z","producer":"crq-runner-app","repo":"camerontaylor/cq-toolkit","type":"crq-run"},"subject_id":"459a3c6e9123e37cf4b3bafa52986ab893229a9a62b3361e08bc14d384fad28d","target":"62bcb3bbc018132ef8a962683eb2eeb798698c24","target_tree":"7e3bc6040d8da1acb2564424b853efe795537180"},"schema":"cq.review-ledger/v1","source_key":"camerontaylor/cq-toolkit:crq-runner-app:backfill-459a3c6e9123e37cf4b3bafa52986ab893229a9a62b3361e08bc14d384fad28d-g0-20261116T045216Z"}